==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Slavic|ljudъ|lang=sh|people, men}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|h₁lewdʰ-|lang=sh}}.

===Noun===
{{sh-noun|g=m|head=ljȗdi|r|људи|љу̑ди}} (singular: {{l|sh|čovjek|čȍvjek}} / {{l|sh|čovek|čȍvek}})

# [[people]], [[men]]
#: Dva ''čovjeka'' su išla cestom — ''Two '''men''' walked down the street.''
#: Pet ''ljudi'' je išlo cestom. — ''Five '''people''' walked down the street.''

====Declension====
{{sh-decl-noun
|čȍvjek|ljȗdi
|čovjeka|ljúdī
|čovjeku|ljudima
|čovjeka|ljude
|čovječe|ljudi
|čovjeku|ljudima
|čovjekom|ljudima}}

====Usage notes====
This plural form takes suppletive stem in the singular, as can be seen in the declension table. Old dual forms have been preserved in the counting for 2, 3, 4 (also in 11, 12, 13, 14 etc.) which bind plural form of {{term|čovjek|čȍvjek|lang=sh}} / {{term|čovek|čȍvek|lang=sh}}.

